  "slug": "decoding-codes-88bf",
  "summary": "Eight preprints from mid-November 2026 push qLDPC decoding toward real-time accuracy, alongside code designs for fixed-connectivity hardware.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is decoding quantum LDPC codes at high accuracy within real-time budgets. SCOPE, a physics-informed parallel decoder, reports a logical error rate of 4.82e-10 on the [[144,12,12]] BB code with 173.8 ns latency. TEMPO-BP adapts per-variable memory strength through local feedback and lowers logical failure rates versus BP+OSD and Relay-BP. TCBP-JOBS learns calibrated fault probabilities on GPUs and matches Tesseract accuracy. A hybrid sliding-window decoder for trapped-ion noise uses soft-output confidence to switch windows, outperforming BP-LSD. Parity push post-selection rejects unreliable shots in a decoder-agnostic way, and non-binary detector error models improve belief propagation under circuit-level noise. Code design contributes Armillary codes with rates above 1/2 for fixed-connectivity superconducting hardware and rate-optimal distance-3 and distance-4 color codes.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
